===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|res iudicata}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|la|rēs||thing, matter, affair}} and {{m|la|jūdicata}}, feminine nominative singular form of {{m|la|jūdicatus}}, past participle of {{m|la|jūdico||judge}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|res judicatae|nolinkhead=1}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} A legal claim that has already been [[decide]]d in another [[lawsuit]] or proceeding, and therefore must be [[dismiss]]ed.
# {{lb|en|legal}} The legal doctrine that claims that a case already decided in a proceeding may not be brought in any later proceeding.

